cells:
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "Problem : mysql takes lots of time to upload data .       \r

      Question : how to upload data in mysql fast ?       \r

      Ans : using the python we learn in sqlalchemy."
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: Today we use the two databases  first is flipcard and secons in
      sql_cx_live aor uska andr tables.
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "## What are SQL Joins \r

      In SQL join is way to combine data from two or more database tables based
      on a related column between them .        \r

      Joins are used when to want to query information that is
      distributed   across multiple tables in a database. and the information we
      need is not contained in a single table.By Joining tables  together ,we
      want to create a virtual table that contain all the information we need in
      our query\r\n"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "join ka use karega aap apna database ma two tables ko jod sakta ho yadi
      unka bitch same column ha tho       \r

      kyu chaya hota ha join ?        \r

      uska answer ha apka jo information chaya vo ek column ma na hokar
      multiples tables ma hota es situation ma tho apko dono,thino ya multiple
      tables ko join karna hoga jis sa ek temporary table form hoga aor aap us
      table ka andr sa information extract kar sakta ho."
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "## slide 2 table "
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "Manager Ask Question :      \r

      har user na kitna order place kiya ha ?         \r

      deko user_name alga table ma ha order_id alag table ma ha        \r

      Join ka crietra (condition)     \r

      jin two tables ko aap join kar raha ho unka bitch ek `common column` hona
      chaya      \r

      tho user_id dono columns ma common ha abba huma complete information mil
      jayega "
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "interseting and curious question bacho wala ?       \r

      why if we store all information in a single table so we do not need
      joins       \r

      what is the problem in it . \r

      apko samjan padega\r

      what is the requirement that we need multiple tables and perform joins "
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "\r

      asa karta ha sari information ko ek hi big table ma store kar leta ha tho
      huma join karna ki jarruat hi nahi padegai.       \r

      lakin kya asa requriement ha ki huma information ko multiple table ma
      store karna padta ha      \r

      yadi aap ya samaj gaya why data is store in multiple tables tho apko RDBMS
      ma relational samaj aa jayeaga. kyu multiple tables hota ha aor vo apas ma
      related hota ha "
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "Reasons         \r

      - Data reducancy = deko ya data repeat ho raha ha and memory ma vo faltu
      ma jada space lega\r

      - update anomly = example aap bharat person na apna location change kar
      liya ahamedabad sa delhi kar liya . deko aap apko database ma change karna
      hoga manually kitna lamba task ha ya .\r

      - normalisation (stucture and classification ) har ek entity ko padekta ho
      aor alag rakta = deko phala users ka information alag tha orders ka
      infromation alag tha or vo well organised tha. yadi apko edit karna ha tho
      aap asani sa kar sakt aho jis sa memory ma jada space occuply nahi ho raha
      "
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "so we learn about data ko multiple table ma store karna kitna jarrui
      ha         \r

      now information multiple tables ma divided ha .         \r

      agar yadi apko information chaya tho apko join lagana padega "
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "# Types of Join\r

      ![alt text](image.png)"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: first hum theortically deka ga fir baad ma pratically una karega.
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: actually we study it in pandas class when we study pandas mergeing this
      class is vary similar their are four major types of join .
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "## Cross join\r\nCartesian product"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "cartesian product kyu kiya jada ha ?        \r

      taki hum all possible combinton mil jaya"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "for example . "
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "$A = \\set{1,2} \\newline\r

      B  = \\set{3,4} \\newline\r

      \\text{The Cartesian product} \\newline\r

      A * B = \\set{(1,3),(1,4),(2,3),(2,4)}\r

      \ $"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "When to use cross join(caretsina product)\r

      - test data\r

      - generate all possible combinations"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: see animaion on inofys slide websitee
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "## inner join "
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "very important aor sabsa jada aap yahi use karoga .     \r

      \ inner join = join based on common column . aap uni columns ko rakoga
      jisma values hoa\r

      \ The inner join retures only the rows from both tables jo condition ko
      satify karta ha . \r

      \ aap uni rows ko rakoga jisma value dono ma true ho. aor false ko reject
      karta ha \r\n"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: venn diagram is intersection.
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: see slide 5 tables
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "We have two tables emplye and departemnt "
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: see the animation of it.
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "left is first table         \r

      right is second table "
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "## left join\r\nslide 6\r\n"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "aap abhi bhi inner join matching condition dekta ho sath ma aap left
      wala table ki values bhi aati ha left also known as(first) .
      so          \r

      left join = common + left"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "example tim divas left side ma tha .agar inner join hota ho nahi ata
      lakin left join ma vo ayaega . "
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "## Right join \r\nslide 7"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "ya ha tik left wala sa ulta aap inner join ki mathcing conditon rakta
      sakth ma right wala "
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "apko department 4 and 5 bhi dika ha "
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "## full outer join \r

      return the all matching rows from both the left and right table .also give
      non mathcing rows from both the table    "
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "slide 8 "
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "# pratical code"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: most of the time common column is primary key
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "hum ek sample data par kam karega\r

      - users ka data \r

      - memebers ka data . ki ya users kis group ka part ha\r

      - groups data . hamra paas 4 groups ha you can think of 4 whastups group
      ha  "
    metadata: {}
